# Hand-written minimal allowlist for the fedora-native chroot (see driver-build/03-touch-input.md).
# ONLY grants node perms for input + the single DRM node this SoC exposes.
# Deliberately NOT the stock 50-udev-default.rules or any other stock rule file --
# those also chmod/chown/rename real Android tty, serial, sound, and network
# nodes shared via the bind-mounted /dev, which would corrupt Android's view.
#
# 2026-09-17 fix (live-tested, caused real drift once): NO GROUP=/OWNER=
# assignment. GROUP="input"/"video" resolves against the CHROOT's own
# /etc/group (gid 104/39 here), which has NO relationship to Android's
# AID-based group numbers on the real, shared /dev nodes (Android's actual
# ownership is "system:input" via AID_SYSTEM/AID_INPUT, not these
# chroot-local numbers). Applying GROUP= silently reassigned live Android
# device nodes to meaningless local gids and broke Android's own
# touchscreen/DRM access until manually chown'd back. MODE=0660 is also
# strictly unnecessary (these nodes are already 0660 by default) but kept as
# an explicit, harmless no-op — our compositor runs as root anyway, which
# bypasses DAC checks entirely, so no permission grant is actually needed
# here. The real requirement this file (+ 60-input-id.rules) serves is
# populating udev's device DATABASE with ID_INPUT* classification tags,
# which is what libinput's enumeration actually reads — not file permissions.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", MODE="0660"
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card0", MODE="0660"

# 2026-09-18 night fix: mutter (unlike labwc/wlroots) enumerates DRM cards via
# g_udev_enumerator_add_match_tag(enumerator, "seat") (meta-udev.c,
# meta_udev_list_drm_devices) -- a tag real systems get for free from
# systemd's own 71-seat.rules, which this minimal chroot rule set never
# included. Without it mutter finds zero candidate GPUs ("Failed to setup:
# No GPUs found") even though the node exists and passes every other check
# in meta_udev_is_drm_device(). Database-only (TAG+= never touches file
# mode/owner), same safety envelope as the MODE= line above.
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card0", TAG+="seat"
